   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "«Ter» + past participle",
     "texto": [
      "The compound perfect is formed with **ter** in the present + participle: **tenho lido** (I have been reading), **tens comido** (you have been eating), **tem vivido** (he / she has been living). With **ter**, the participle does not change."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Use: repeated or continued actions",
     "texto": [
      "**Tenho estudado muito ultimamente** (I've been studying a lot lately). For a one-off visit already made, say **Já visitei Coimbra** (I have already visited Coimbra), not *já tenho visitado*. Also common are **ainda não fui** and **nunca visitei**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Pronoun with «já»",
     "texto": [
      "In **Já a visitei** (I've already visited her / it), the unstressed pronoun comes before the verb. Learn this common combination; the pronoun's position also depends on other elements in the sentence."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
